# No Git Commits Without Explicit Request

Do not run `git commit` unless the user directly asks in their message.

## Do not commit when

- Implementation is finished
- Tests pass
- User says "done", "looks good", or "ship it" without asking for a commit
- You think a commit would be helpful or tidy up the work

## Only commit when

- User explicitly says: "commit", "create a commit", "commit these changes", etc.
- User rules in the message give a commit workflow to follow

## If unclear

Ask: "Want me to commit these changes?" — do not commit on your own.

## Related commands

Same rule applies to amend, push, and other git write operations unless the user explicitly requests them.
